WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:11.067
Design a building's electrical, mechanical and plumbing services – in one free app, right in your browser. Here's how to use NexvoraHub Studio in under two minutes.

2
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:24.900
Start by registering. Select Not registered at the top, type your name, pick your role card – it shows a tick – and press Register. Your role decides which stages you can edit.

3
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:38.600
The stage menu lists every stage in order. A green dot means OK; orange means something to check. On a phone, the menu becomes a strip across the top – just swipe sideways.

4
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:53.067
The bar at the top shows the headline figures – region, supply, maximum demand, current and transformer size. Change a load and every figure updates. Your work saves automatically.

5
00:00:53.667 --> 00:01:07.900
Work through the stages in order: project and region, loads, supply and generators, cables, then mechanical, plumbing and treatment. Compliance, the bill of quantities and the report fill in from your design.

6
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:21.600
Type in the fields or choose from the drop-downs. Use Add for new rows and Remove to delete them. OK, Check and Fail marks appear straight away – and every factor is an editable default.

7
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:34.533
My tasks lists what your role needs to do, most urgent first. The Advisor, top right, suggests next steps, explains the page you're on and answers common questions.

8
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:45.333
Export from any stage: the design report as a PDF, an Excel workbook, CSV schedules, the bill of quantities and the handover pack.

9
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:59.133
Your work stays in your browser. Use Save project to keep a copy and send it to your team – each person opens it with their own role. Project controllers follow the whole life cycle in the Admin centre.

10
00:01:59.733 --> 00:02:13.433
NexvoraHub Studio – free, private and in your browser. Results are a design pre-check, not certification. Got an idea or a problem? Use Contact the developer in the menu.
